-- title:
--   Both actual Gaussian and full-negative-mark stopped gains have zero mean on every positive-clock initial event
-- statement:
--   At an original finite-range bounded stopping time, the genuine Gaussian R and full compensated negative-mark Jfull are integrable and initially conditionally centred; hence their expected stopped values each vanish on every initial-information event intersected with {tau != 0}. Both fullmark sources and the exact original discounted terminal plus full Stieltjes cash reward are retained. This is the precise physical eventwise two-noise cancellation needed by the Open positive-clock ledger.

